Description: hw/gpio: Add the i.MX21 GPIO controller
 Six 32-pin ports sharing one interrupt, with edge and level interrupt
 sensing and the port interrupt mask. This is the i.MX1-style GPIO block,
 not the i.MX31 one.
 .
 Each pin also has an output line, numbered like its input (port * 32 +
 pin), carrying the pin's level: the data register for pins configured
 as outputs, the level driven from outside for inputs. A line changes
 only when its pin's level does, after a register write, an input change
 or a reset. The Chumby Classic's sensor card is selected this way: the
 stock driver (chumby_accel.c) drives PD28 and PD27 by hand through the
 port's data register, and the card decodes them into its chip selects.
